      "clauses": [
        {
          "claim": "Original polynomial and tower bounds",
          "comparison": "Current theorem87–103 gives the same total292890231905 variables, degree<tw7 and coefficient magnitudes<tw8. It explicitly permits dummy ambient variables and means ordinary embedded integers. The assembly159–207 keeps G,M,H,PC,C,B as proof inputs; the announcement cannot serve as evidence for any of them."
        },
        {
          "claim": "Minimum defining degree four",
          "comparison": "The lower theorem12788–12791 applies to total degree including the input. Existence of a quartic provides the matching upper bound. The current minimum and its two explicit incoming connections are retained; the bound is not inferred from the abstract alone."
        },
        {
          "claim": "Historical411/394 polynomial claims",
          "comparison": "These conclusions remain exactly as the Version13 baseline theorem21898–21916:394variables6338monomials and coefficient16*3^(2^26), and411variables6388monomials with coefficients<2^3247. The current abstract no longer advertises these as records. Their retained proof and finite-count inputs remain separate; this mapping does not replace them with the different Version14 artifacts."
        },
        {
          "claim": "Current314/299 polynomial claims",
          "comparison": "Current abstract51–58 agrees with theorem22761–22781:299variables6630monomials and coefficient186624*3^(2^26), and314variables6672monomials with coefficients<2^6496 and compact decimal table264430bytes. C=3^(2^25) is fixed, not quantified. Current theorem and its existing proof graph supply the new claims; there is no assertion that the old and new tables are identical."
        },
        {
          "claim": "Mazur, universal rational polynomial and HTP equivalence",
          "comparison": "The current corollary section expressly consumes equality of the ordinary-integer zero projection. It does not prove that equality. Universal parameters e,n are ordinary natural integers, using disjoint witness blocks. The HTP result consumes the universal polynomial. Existing independent corollary applications and their incoming main-theorem premise are retained."
        }
      ],
      "comparison": "An announcement/current-version reconciliation, not a supplier theorem. The entire initial compound statement is preserved verbatim, including its warning that announced results require later proof. The historical411/394 conclusions are located in their retained baseline, and the separate current314/299 announcement is located in its actual theorem. No arithmetic dependency is discharged by the abstract or by this map.",
      "scope": "Exact clause-to-current mapping, pending independent comparison; this is not proof or release acceptance.",
      "remaining": [
        "All explicit incoming premises of the referenced applications remain governed by final source-first coverage.",
        "This mapping does not independently reverify the coefficient tables or arithmetic ancestors."
